          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "OpenAI may be building a smartphone with AI agents replacing apps, in talks with MediaTek and Qualcomm",
            "articleSection": "Daily Utility",
            "abstract": "Industry analyst Ming-Chi Kuo reports that OpenAI is in discussions with chipmakers MediaTek and Qualcomm, and manufacturer Luxshare, to develop a smartphone in which AI agents replace traditional apps. The device would represent a radical reimagining of how people interact with their phones, with autonomous AI performing tasks instead of discrete applications. OpenAI is also reported to be developing earbuds, suggesting a broader consumer hardware push beyond software and APIs.",
            "url": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/27/openai-could-be-making-a-phone-with-ai-agents-replacing-apps/",
            "publisher": {
